\begin{definition} (\cite[Definition 2.3]{KuperbergWeaver2012MemAMS}).
Let $\mathcal M\subset  \mathcal{B(H)$ be a von Neumann algebra. A family $\mathbf{V}=(\mathcal{V_t)_{t\geq 0}$ of weak$^*$-closed operator systems\footnote{A closed subspace of $\mathcal{B(H)$ is an \emph{operator system} if it is self-adjoint and contains $1_H$.} in $\mathcal{B(H)$ is called a \emph{quantum metric on $\mathcal M \subset  \mathcal{B(H)$} if
